  "notes": "STRUCTURE:\n{帰|き} (return) + {省|せい} (reflect; visit parents). The character {省|せい} here carries its classical meaning of visiting one's parents.\n\nUSAGE:\n{帰省|きせい} is used both as a noun and as a する verb ({帰省|きせい}する). It specifically refers to returning to one's hometown or parents' home, not just going home in general. The {帰省|きせい}ラッシュ (homecoming rush) during major holidays like お{盆|ぼん}, {年末年始|ねんまつねんし}, and ゴールデンウィーク is a well-known phenomenon in Japan, causing heavy congestion on highways and trains.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {帰省|きせい}する: to return to one's hometown\n- {帰省|きせい}ラッシュ: homecoming rush\n- {帰省|きせい}{先|さき}: hometown destination\n- {帰省|きせい}{土産|みやげ}: souvenirs brought when visiting home",
